pokeplatinum-vblanktasks.patch (tools/pokeplat_gen.py applies the patches in name order): room for the V-blank tasks
one frame schedules. The DS runs gSystem.vBlankTaskMgr's tasks in its V-blank interrupt, which also fires during a
long load; the PC runs them only at the game's V-blank wait. Entering the field schedules one BindModelTextureSysTaskCB
(simple3d.c) per map model in one frame: the 32 slots filled, and the next SysTask_ExecuteOnVBlank returned NULL, so the
map objects' texture upload task (ov5_021ECE40.c's ov5_021EE1AC) never ran: their textures were discarded without an
upload and the player's billboard drew whatever was in its VRAM (pl9). 256 slots where a pointer is 8 bytes.

diff --git a/src/system.c b/src/system.c
index 7668a409c..cab14a543 100644
--- a/src/system.c
+++ b/src/system.c
@@ -13,5 +13,14 @@
 
 #define MAIN_TASK_MAX        160
+#include <stdint.h>
+
+// The DS runs the V-blank tasks in its V-blank interrupt, which also fires in the middle of a long load (the field
+// schedules one texture bind per map model), so the 32 slots drain while the load goes on. The PC runs them only at
+// the game's V-blank wait, after the whole load: room for every task one frame can schedule.
+#if UINTPTR_MAX > 0xFFFFFFFFu
+#define VBLANK_TASK_MAX      256
+#else
 #define VBLANK_TASK_MAX      32
+#endif
 #define POST_VBLANK_TASK_MAX 32
 #define PRINT_TASK_MAX       4
